  <title>Writing</title>

  <section id="composer">
    <title>The composer</title>
    <p>
      <gui>New Post</gui>, or Ctrl+N, opens the composer. It checks spelling,
      completes <gui>@mentions</gui> and hashtags as you type.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="media">
    <title>Media</title>
    <p>
      Attach media by choosing it in the composer, by pasting or dragging
      it in, or by taking a screenshot from the clipboard.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="sending">
    <title>Sending and drafts</title>
    <p>
      Ctrl+Enter sends. Escape closes the composer without sending.
      Drafts are kept for you: close the composer with something
      half-written and Babble offers it back on the next launch.
    </p>
    <p>
      To send a post later, press <gui>Schedule Post</gui> in the
      composer's header bar and pick a date and time at least five minutes
      ahead. The chosen time is shown above the post, and <gui>Post</gui>
      becomes <gui>Schedule</gui>; <gui>Clear Schedule</gui> sends it now
      instead. Scheduled posts are listed under <gui>Scheduled Posts</gui>
      in the main menu, where they can be edited, rescheduled or deleted.
    </p>
  </section>

</page>